\title{netLOO: Leave-One-Out Contribution Analysis for Multi-Temporal Bipartite Networks}
\description{
A dataset-agnostic toolkit for multi-temporal bipartite network analysis (e.g. plant-pollinator webs sampled across years or conditions). Computes per-network structural metrics, species persistence and turnover, pairwise interaction beta diversity, null models, rarefaction, and a leave-one-out contribution analysis that quantifies how much each time point uniquely contributes to the pooled metaweb, relative to what would be expected. Generalizes the analysis pipeline from Medel & Fontúrbel's blooming-desert plant-pollinator study to any set of bipartite networks sampled at three or more time points.
}
